{
  "_comment": [
    "Number/scale lexicon for income parsing — DATA, not code.",
    "Written in real Unicode (no backslash-u escape sequences): the previous",
    "parser hard-coded them per language inside regex alternations, which is how a",
    "Devanagari letter silently ended up in the Bengali entry.",
    "Adding a language = adding one block here. `validate_lexicon()` checks that",
    "every entry's characters belong to that language's declared scripts, and the",
    "test suite re-runs that check, so a wrong-script glyph fails CI instead of",
    "silently mis-parsing a student's income.",
    "Scales are 10^n: crore = 10,000,000 (Indian) — previously unsupported."
  ],
  "version": 2,
  "scales": {
    "crore": 10000000,
    "lakh": 100000,
    "thousand": 1000
  },
  "languages": {
    "en": {
      "name": "English",
      "scripts": ["Latin"],
      "words": {
        "crore": ["crore", "crores", "cr"],
        "lakh": ["lakh", "lakhs", "lac", "lacs", "lakh(s)", "l"],
        "thousand": ["thousand", "thousands", "k"]
      }
    },
